===Etymology===
From {{inh|en|enm|pece}}, {{m|enm|peece}}, {{m|enm|peice}}, from {{der|en|fro|piece}}, from {{der|en|LL.|petia}}, {{m|la|pettia}}, possibly from {{der|en|cel-gau|*pettyā}}, from {{der|en|cel-pro|*kʷezdis|t=piece, portion, quota}}; doublet of {{cog|en|fit}}, {{m|en|fytte}}, {{m|en|fytt||musical piece, chapter}}, {{cog|is|fit||web}}, {{cog|de|Fitze||skein}}, from {{cog|goh|*fitjâ}}. Compare {{cog|cy|peth}}, {{cog|br|pez||thing}}, {{cog|ga|cuid}}. Compare {{cog|fr|pièce}}, {{cog|pt|peça}}, {{cog|es|pieza}}, {{cog|it|pezza}}, {{cog|it|pezzo}}.

